P-6: config/budgets.yaml's `public` section, the relay's public request cap (spec 001 FR-033; plan.md §14, P-6;
tasks.md T105; ADR 0029). For the Author's hand: config/budgets.yaml is human-only (ADR 0017).

Built by the implementer agent on feat/001-w1 from plain copies: `git show 7c5f1259:config/budgets.yaml` into $TMPDIR,
the section appended, then `diff -u` with a/ and b/ labels after this preamble. Never `git apply`; no protected file
written into any worktree.

Each figure is left blank and marked as the Author's. Before he applies it (T114), he writes his four figures where
the patch says "the Author's figure", and the same figures, with the date, into ADR 0029's Decision 4. With a figure
blank the gateway's validator refuses the file (rule B10, naming each key) and the relay refuses to start, so this
patch applies only with his figures in it. The bounds the validator holds them to: requests_per_minute 1 to 600,
burst 1 to 600 and at most requests_per_minute, requests_per_day 1 to 100000 and at least requests_per_minute,
in_flight 1 to 256.

Applies to config/budgets.yaml as of 7c5f1259, with `patch -p1`, first in the stack, since no other patch touches the file.

--- a/config/budgets.yaml
+++ b/config/budgets.yaml
@@ -26,3 +26,17 @@
   # turns and characters of conversation a request carries, a twin call's input bound (also its reservation's), and
   # its output cap.
   twin:        { turn_max_chars: 600, history_max_turns: 8, history_max_chars: 4000, max_input_chars: 32000, max_output_tokens: 300 }
+
+# The relay's public request cap (spec 001 FR-033, FR-042; ADR 0029; contracts/relay-http.md §3, step 3), on the
+# tunnel end, before any gateway: per address, from the address CloudFront supplies, a token bucket of `burst`
+# refilled at `requests_per_minute`, and at most `requests_per_day` a UTC day; and across every address at most
+# `in_flight` requests forwarded and not yet answered. Held in memory only, for at most one UTC day. Each figure is
+# the Author's (P-6; tasks.md T114): the relay refuses to start, and the gateway's validator refuses the file, while
+# one is blank, naming each key.
+public:
+  per_address:
+    requests_per_minute:   # the Author's figure
+    burst:                 # the Author's figure
+    requests_per_day:      # the Author's figure
+  global:
+    in_flight:             # the Author's figure
